# The study: papered wall, boards, a window onto dusk and a lamp. 240x175,
# drawn at 4x to fill the 960x700 window exactly.
#
# Two light sources opposing each other — cool from the window, warm from the
# lamp — which is the whole reason this palette has both night-* and lamp-*.
# A flat bust pasted onto a flat room looks pasted on; a bust with somewhere to
# sit between two lights looks like it is in the room.
#
# The lamp's pool on the wall is Bayer-dithered out at its edge rather than
# hard-edged, because a hard-edged pool of light reads as a painted circle.
name visualnovel-room
size 240 175
key W room-1
key w room-0-shadow
key R room-2
key F room-0-shadow
key f room-1
key o outline
key N night-0
key M night-1
key L night-2-hilite
key G lamp-2-glow
key g lamp-1
key h lamp-0
pixels
